# Do not delete this file, and do not "simplify" it away.
#
# Our .gitignore excludes media/ and public-data/library.json on purpose - the
# audio is the user's own, and it does not belong in a public git repo. But
# those are exactly the files the deployed app needs: without them Railway
# ships a working player with an empty library and no audio at all.
#
# CONFIRMED IN PRACTICE (railway CLI v5.23.2): .railwayignore does NOT override
# .gitignore just by existing - `railway up` applies .gitignore rules on top of
# it regardless. The only thing that actually stops that is passing
# --no-gitignore on every deploy:
#
#   railway up --no-gitignore
#
# Forgetting that flag silently deploys an empty library with no audio and no
# error of any kind - it looks like a successful deploy. Verify after every
# deploy with: curl <url>/api/library (after logging in) and confirm it is not
# {"tracks":[],"playlists":[]}.
#
# This file's own listed patterns (build junk, sample fixtures) still apply
# normally on top of that flag.

node_modules
.git
.gitignore

